  "starterCode": "import math, numpy as np\n\ndef dl_positional_encoding(X: list, theta: float = 10000.0) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport math, numpy as np\n\ndef dl_positional_encoding(X: list, theta: float = 10000.0) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    N, D = arr.shape\n    out = np.zeros_like(arr)\n    for p in range(N):\n        for i in range(D // 2):\n            ang = p * (1.0 / (theta ** (2 * i / D)))\n            c, s = math.cos(ang), math.sin(ang)\n            out[p, 2*i] = arr[p, 2*i] * c - arr[p, 2*i+1] * s\n            out[p, 2*i+1] = arr[p, 2*i] * s + arr[p, 2*i+1] * c\n    return np.round(out, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
